{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared normalisation contract for section parity dumps.",
    "",
    "The Markdown report and the app render the same content in different",
    "markup (Markdown vs DOM). To diff them we project both through the SAME",
    "normalisation rules. Two implementations exist:",
    "  - birding/parity_dump.py          normalize() / entry_key()",
    "  - birding-app/www/index.html      pdNormalize() / pdEntryKey()",
    "",
    "Both are asserted against this fixture, so they cannot drift:",
    "  - birding/tests/parity/test_normalize.py",
    "  - birding-app/tests/normalize.test.js",
    "",
    "'in' is raw Markdown or raw HTML, 'text' is the normalised plain text,",
    "'key' is the diff identity (leading label, decoration stripped)."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "why": "markdown link unwraps to its text",
      "in": "[Tufted Puffin](https://ebird.org/species/tufpuf/US-WA) — **11.7 mi**",
      "text": "Tufted Puffin - 11.7 mi",
      "key": "tufted puffin"
    },
    {
      "why": "html link unwraps the same way",
      "in": "<a href=\"https://ebird.org/species/tufpuf/US-WA\">Tufted Puffin</a> &mdash; <b>11.7 mi</b>",
      "text": "Tufted Puffin - 11.7 mi",
      "key": "tufted puffin"
    },
    {
      "why": "app list row: count badge, photo slot, name and meta divs",
      "in": "<span class=\"count\">\u00d711</span><div class=\"name\"><span class=\"thumb\" data-bird=\"Tufted Puffin\"><img class=\"birdpic\" src=\"x.jpg\"></span>Tufted Puffin</div><div class=\"meta\">Edmonds Waterfront \u00b7 Jul 26 10:50 am</div>",
      "text": "\u00d711 \u00b7 Tufted Puffin \u00b7 Edmonds Waterfront \u00b7 Jul 26 10:50 am",
      "key": "tufted puffin"
    },
    {
      "why": "report table row keyed past the rank column",
      "in": "1 \u00b7 [Stanwood Water Treatment Plant](https://ebird.org/hotspot/L343249) ([\ud83d\uddfa](https://maps.example)) \u00b7 53 \u00b7 34.4 mi",
      "text": "1 \u00b7 Stanwood Water Treatment Plant \u00b7 53 \u00b7 34.4 mi",
      "key": "stanwood water treatment plant"
    },
    {
      "why": "emoji-only link text leaves no empty brackets behind",
      "in": "Edmonds Waterfront ([\ud83d\uddfa](https://www.google.com/maps))",
      "text": "Edmonds Waterfront",
      "key": "edmonds waterfront"
    },
    {
      "why": "new-bird marker and emphasis are decoration, not content",
      "in": "\ud83c\udd95 **[White Wagtail](https://ebird.org/species/whiwag/US-WA)**",
      "text": "White Wagtail",
      "key": "white wagtail"
    },
    {
      "why": "images are dropped entirely",
      "in": "![Birdiest checklists map](maps/2026-07-26-birdiest-checklists.svg) Stanwood",
      "text": "Stanwood",
      "key": "stanwood"
    },
    {
      "why": "hyphenated species names survive the ' - ' split",
      "in": "[Black-backed Woodpecker](https://ebird.org/species/bkbwoo) — 38.6 mi",
      "text": "Black-backed Woodpecker - 38.6 mi",
      "key": "black backed woodpecker"
    },
    {
      "why": "html entities decode",
      "in": "Kent Ponds &amp; Marsh &#183; 42",
      "text": "Kent Ponds & Marsh \u00b7 42",
      "key": "kent ponds marsh"
    },
    {
      "why": "collapsible report cell keeps its summary content",
      "in": "<details><summary>2</summary>Jul 25 8:11 pm (1) \u00b7 <a href=\"u\">Stanwood</a></details>",
      "text": "2 \u00b7 Jul 25 8:11 pm (1) \u00b7 Stanwood",
      "key": "jul 25 8 11 pm 1"
    },
    {
      "why": "runs of separators collapse to one",
      "in": "A \u00b7\u00b7 B  \u00b7   \u00b7 C",
      "text": "A \u00b7 B \u00b7 C",
      "key": "a"
    },
    {
      "why": "non-breaking spaces are ordinary spaces",
      "in": "Ruff\u00a0\u00a0\u2014\u00a0Pacific Co.",
      "text": "Ruff - Pacific Co.",
      "key": "ruff"
    },
    {
      "why": "empty input stays empty",
      "in": "   ",
      "text": "",
      "key": ""
    }
  ]
}
